A||||15||Jimmy||First time Drag Racing||||1||
Z||000000||Jimmy||10-08-2001||12:37 AM||||Scanner doesn't work so I'll type in my slips.<P>1st run<P>R/T 1.087<BR>60' 1.894<BR>330 5.662<BR>1/8 8.753<BR>MPH 80.13<BR>1000 11.434<BR>1/4 13.694<BR>MPH 99.12<P>2nd Run<P>R/T .968<BR>60' 1.867<BR>330 5.644<BR>1/8 8.752<BR>MPH 79.66<BR>1000 11.432<BR>1/4 13.736<BR>MPH 97.59<P>3rd Run<P>R/T .927<BR>60' 1.908<BR>330 5.687<BR>1/8 8.776<BR>MPH 80.17<BR>1000 11.452<BR>1/4 13.692<BR>MPH 99.85<P>Guess I'm not overly excited about my slips but I got to start somewhere.  <P>About the only thing I was happy about was my 60' times.  Those will be better when I fix my carb(my car would just LAUNCH off the line, BOG, Then go again). Considering my carb would bog every time I launched, I thought my 60' times were respectable.<P>I need to get a clutch or pressure plate that can hold in 4th gear.  I was able to grab rubber in second and third before, now I can't even get second if I try.<P>Every time I shifted it seemed as if the engine would hold its RPM(clutch slip?) then drop to the proper RPM.  Fourth was the worst, had to back off of WOT and let it grab then ease in on the throttle again.<P>I'll work on my reaction time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I did have A LOT of fun, met a lot of nice people, and will be going back next weekend.  I want to tweak the motor this week and go back to the strip to get some more runs under my belt before the winter.<P>Can't wait to find a better clutch/pressure plate and redo my motor.<P>I'll post new times after next weekend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I did meet a guy who runs a 9 second 87 Fiero GT.  He hopes to run High 8s next year. Its engine is in the front.<P>Jim<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT||||reg||1
