Z||000006||Jimmy||10-08-2001||11:36 AM||||My 350 is a stock rebuild for the most part, no real go fast goodies yet. I don't know the cam specs but its your basic RV type cam, flattop pistons, stock heads rebuilt and new springs.  Edelbrock performer intake and a used and abused 600 CFM Edelbrock. ramhorn exhaust 2 1/4".  Dual friction center force clutch.<P>Did I mention my motor got sugared?  Had to pull my carb apart and wash it in hot water. <P>My engine builder told me these motors usually make around 265HP and 310 ftlbs of torque.  I wonder if mine was even approaching those numbers.<P>BTW, I have 5000 miles on this setup, drive it to work thru rushhour and back everyday, never been stranded, and have loved every mile of it.  Drove it to the strip(200 there and back), dragged it, then drove it back home with no problems.<P>I have big plans for the motor this winter.  I just have to figure out a clutch for this system.  Maybe 1fst2m6 has a recommendation? I know the quartermaster setup will work(California kid) but I would like to try and use the standard setup.  <P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jimmy||10-08-2001||11:54 AM||||Yeah. like others have said, I run full interior, spare tire, jack, and junk in the trunk.  <P>My tires are stock 215 60R 15.  I do have a set of 8" Goodyear slicks however.<P>I didn't take a very serious approach to getting a good time at the strip.  Didn't think of removing stuff or trying better tires.  That's all changed now, I'm hooked.  Its a lot of fun and can't believe I waited all year(especially until my car ran worse) to get to the strip.<P>Jim||||reg||1
